    "explanation": "Both of you: the disputed SGD 4.00 no-show fee is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable. This turns on location, not on how long the driver waited.\n\nARRIVAL AND DWELL. The pickup is a LARGE_VENUE zone ('NEX Serangoon, Tower B ride-hail pickup'), so the POL-NS-02 arrival radius is 120 m. The driver's own GPS trace places all 34 of his fixes (13:05:00 to 13:10:30, every one at 0.0 km/h) at 219.8 m from the pin — zero qualifying in-geofence fixes, longest in-geofence run 0.0 s. POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails and the fee is not chargeable under POL-NS-01. Because the driver was nonetheless stationary for the required 300-second dwell (about 330 s of continuous fixes) at a point outside the 120 m radius but well inside the 400 m ceiling POL-NS-03 sets, POL-NS-03 governs and refunds the fee in full. POL-NS-06 points the same way (0 s of in-geofence dwell against a 300 s minimum), and its limb (i) accumulation route is unavailable: there are no intervals to sum, and the only advisory on file (EV-ADVIS-09105-01) is MISSING with weight 0.0 — I rely on that absence, which POL-GEN-02 makes citable, not on any content. The SGD 4.00 charge itself is correct: it is the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00), so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises.\n\nWHO BEARS THE LOSS. The chat log decides this. The rider wrote at 13:05:05 'I am at Tower B ride-hail pickup, beside the blue sign' and again at 13:06:35 'That is the other entrance. Please come to Tower B.' The driver replied at 13:06:00 that he was at 'the mall taxi stand', and his own statement concedes he waited at a mall entrance and did not move to Tower B before cancelling. Under POL-NS-03 limb (i) the mislocation is attributed to the driver and his compensation is extinguished. The 3 registered pickup points do not convert this into pin ambiguity, because the rider did name the sub-location, so no POL-NS-03(ii) goodwill arises.\n\nMATTERS RAISED BY THE DRIVER. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: the driver was stationary within the clause's own 300 m carve-out and below 15 km/h, so the 'arrived' marker is not a false arrival and no POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival referral is made — the case falls to POL-NS-03 exactly as that clause directs. The driver's concession that the fee should be refunded is accepted. His point that driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags is context-only under POL-GEN-01 is correct; the anti-farming check reads no_show_terminations_30d (1) against completed_trips_30d (120), far below POL-NS-07's thresholds, so no charge-farming pattern is found and no adverse inference is drawn from his record. POL-NS-07 compensation does not arise in any event, because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied and POL-NS-03 displaces it.\n\nMATTERS RAISED BY THE RIDER. POL-NS-04 is contested: the driver did reply within 120 seconds of the rider's first locating message, though not of the second. The point is academic — whether or not POL-NS-04 additionally exonerates the rider, POL-NS-03 independently produces the same result: full refund, no driver compensation. The rider's rider-presence showing (all 16 fixes ~25 m from the pin, inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius) is noted but adds nothing the location finding does not already give.\n\nINTEGRITY AND ESCALATION. No artifact is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08: no clock skew (the arrived event lands on a fix timestamp), no trace gap (max_gap_sec 0.0, 34 fixes), no chat defect (4 messages matching the trip record's count, no msg_id gap), no fare defect. The deciding facts are carried by EV-GPS-09105, EV-TRIP-09105, EV-CHAT-09105 and EV-FARE-09105, all at weight 1.0, and the driver's counterparty statement is a concession against his own interest that independently supports the location finding. No POL-NS-09 limb fires: confidence is well above the 0.70 floor, no two admissible artifacts conflict, the counterparty-dispute counters are both